    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nSince the response DTOs are generated at build time from `openapi.yml` and populated through MapStruct, the change spans three files following the existing `membershipNumber` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` is generated with the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a stateless, seed-independent helper `CheckDigit.of(String customerCode)` that applies the standard Luhn algorithm over the decimal digits of the customer code (ignoring the hyphen/letter separators), returning `null` when the code is absent. Its logic mirrors the test's `luhn(...)` exactly.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `@Mapping` expression wiring `checkDigit` to `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`, so it appears on both the create and GET owner responses.\n\nTest results: `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the new `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` acceptance test, the only test class in the project, passes).",
